      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even with low heat soak characteristics, intermittent brake fade or unpredictable pedal feel can occur due to factors like pad wear, clutch release system (CRS) efficiency, and caliper seal integrity. Worn pads, even if producing low temperatures, can still ingest excessive dirt and debris, affecting braking performance. Additionally, a degraded CRS or worn-out caliper seals can cause uneven wear, associated with brake pulsation, and lead to unpredictable pedal feel during sustained heavy braking.",
      "source": "target",
